mode: "100644"
text: "# Scope, distinctions + connections\n\npinterest-pin-design is a **design-craft skill** — it designs the pin's concept, composition, and overlay,\nproduces the **brief**, and plans the **fresh-pin variants**. The agent **designs + briefs + critiques +\nplans**; a **human or image tool makes the raster**; **WoopSocial publishes the finished pin** (image +\ntitle + description + board + link).\n\n## Honest scope (never violate)\n- **The agent** designs the **concept**, the **composition**, the **overlay text**, and the **design\n  brief**, plans the **3–5 fresh variants per URL**, and can **critique a mockup** — but a **HUMAN or an\n  image/design tool** (`ideogram` for in-image text / `canva` / `nano-banana` / a designer) **creates the final\n  raster.** The agent doesn't render the pixels.\n- **WoopSocial publishes** the finished pin — **image + title (≤100) + description + board\n  (`pinterestBoardId`) + link (≤2048)** — and that is ALL it does here: it does **NOT** design, template,\n  or generate the visual. Saves, outbound clicks, and impressions come from **WoopSocial post analytics**, not from\n  **native Pinterest Analytics.**\n- **The words are pinterest-seo's:** the keyword research, the keyword-led title/description, and board\n  names/descriptions. This skill **renders the keyword visually** (the overlay) — it doesn't pick it.\n- **No misleading pins** — the image must promise what the destination delivers (**Pin → Board → Page\n  match**; long clicks rank, bounces punish, and a pin lives ~4 months, so deception compounds against\n  you). **No repin-as-fresh dupes** (a color swap is not a fresh pin; near-identical volume gets\n  suppressed). **No unconsented real-person faces.** **Disclose GenAI imagery** (users can filter it) and\n  **FTC-disclose affiliate pins.** **Never fabricate engagement.** **Verify-quarterly** (formats/feed\n  rendering move — idea pins especially).\n\n## Distinct from its siblings\n- **pinterest-pin-design (this)** — the pin's **VISUAL craft + brief + fresh-variant plan** (2:3, overlay,\n  focal point, brand template, covers).\n- **pinterest-seo** — the **keyword / search-RANKING layer.** **They PAIR:** the keyword goes in the\n  **overlay AND the title** — pinterest-seo picks it, this skill renders it legibly.\n- **pinterest-growth** — the **account strategy** (boards/clusters, cadence, ~72h same-URL spacing,\n  seasonal 45–90-day lead, link-out strategy). It calls for \"3–5 distinct designs per destination\" — this\n  skill is where those designs get made.\n- **design-and-templates** — the **brand template SYSTEM**; the pin template is **one asset type in** that\n  system (its 2:3 1000×1500 slot routes here).\n- **thumbnail-design** — the **same craft for YouTube's 16:9** click decision; different job (click-to-watch\n  vs save-and-click-out), different canvas, different text rules.\n- **ideogram** / **canva** / **nano-banana** / **flux** — **generate/produce the raster** this skill briefs\n  (ideogram especially for the overlay text; flux for backgrounds).\n- **quote-cards-and-text-graphics** / **infographic-and-data-viz** — other single-asset graphic types; a\n  quote card or infographic **repurposed to 2:3 for Pinterest** comes through here for the pin treatment.\n\n## Where this connects\n- **Reads first:** `brand-profile` (palette/fonts/style), the **destination** (the page the pin links to),\n  and the **keyword** from `pinterest-seo`.\n- **Pairs with:** `pinterest-seo` (keyword in the overlay + title), `image-prompt` → `ideogram`/`nano-banana`/\n  `flux` (render the brief), `canva` (template production), `ai-image-editing` (crops/variants/cleanup),\n  `design-and-templates` (the pin template family), `before-after-and-transformation` (honest split-frame\n  pins).\n- **Routes to / from:** `pinterest-growth` (strategy/cadence/boards), `content-recycling` +\n  `cross-platform-repurposing` (which evergreen URLs deserve fresh variants; what gets re-cut to 2:3),\n  `seasonal-and-moment-marketing` (the 45–90-day seasonal window), `competitor-analysis` (preview against\n  the pins ranking for the keyword).\n- **Publishes via:** `scheduling-and-queue → WoopSocial` (pin image + title + description + board + link) +\n  `platform-specs-and-validation` (2:3 checks). **Measures with:** native **Pinterest Analytics** +\n  `analytics-and-reporting` (saves, outbound clicks, impressions). **The raster stays with the image tools/\n  designer; the keyword stays with pinterest-seo; cadence stays with pinterest-growth.**\n"
